# RapidPhotoUpload - Cursor Rules

## Communication Style
- Provide summaries and status updates INTERACTIVELY in chat, not as separate markdown files
- Only create documentation files when explicitly requested or when it's part of the core deliverables
- Focus on taking action and showing results, not documenting every step

## Code & Implementation
- Follow clean code principles (DDD, CQRS, VSA)
- Use the tech stack defined in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
- Test code before marking tasks complete
- Keep commits small and focused

## Progress Tracking
- Update todo list when working on multi-step tasks
- Mark tasks complete as they finish
- Report progress concisely in chat

## File Management
- Don't create *_SUMMARY.md, *_RESULTS.md, or *_COMPLETE.md files unless specifically requested
- Core documentation (README, setup guides, architecture docs) is fine
- Temporary verification scripts and tools are useful

